2024 上海高考英语作文题目
题目：假如你是高三同学李华，开设了英文报刊：排忧解难（TROUBLESHOOTER），一个学生 Lynn 对报
刊提出问题，I really want to do cooking, but my parents never allow me to do it. How can I change their mind? 请
你以该栏目的名义给Lynn回信,内容包括：1.你的建议；2.你的理由。
Dear Lynn,
I understand your desire to cook and your parents' concerns. Here are my suggestions:
First, explain to your parents why cooking is important to you. Emphasize its value as a life skill and a creative
outlet.
Second, offer to start with simple and safe recipes under their supervision. Show them you can be responsible
and follow safety guidelines.
Finally, demonstrate your commitment by reading cookbooks and watching cooking shows. This will prove your
seriousness and may help change their minds.
Best of luck!
Sincerely,
Li Hua
TROUBLESHOOTER
Dear Lynn,
I understand your desire to cook, despite your parents' resistance. To convince them, it is important to address
their concerns and communicate effectively.
Firstly, empathize with their worries about your safety. Assure them that you will prioritize precautions, such as
wearing appropriate attire and handling utensils carefully. Offer to take cooking classes or watch tutorial videos to
show your commitment to learning responsible cooking habits.
Second, highlight the educational and practical benefits of cooking. Explain that it is a valuable life skill,
promoting healthier food choices and fostering creativity and problem-solving abilities.
Finally, involve your parents in the process by suggesting cooking together as a family. This allows them to
witness your progress, share their culinary knowledge, and provide guidance and supervision. It also strengthens
family ties.
Remember to communicate calmly and respectfully, listening to their concerns and addressing them. Present
your case with a well-thought-out plan and emphasize the benefits. With perseverance and understanding, you can
persuade your parents to support your passion for cooking.
Best of luck!
Sincerely,
Li Hua
TROUBLESHOOTER
第1页/共1页
